{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "version": 2,

  "//": [
    "AURA-EVAL — SINGLE-PROJECT, MULTI-SERVICE Vercel deployment.",
    "",
    "Two services are built from this one repository and served on ONE domain:",
    "  1. @vercel/python -> api/index.py     (FastAPI, re-exported from backend/)",
    "  2. @vercel/next   -> frontend/         (Next.js 14 App Router)",
    "",
    "Routing: /api/* is handled by the Python lambda; everything else falls",
    "through to the Next.js build. Because both share an origin, the browser",
    "uses relative URLs, NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL can be left empty, and CORS is a",
    "non-issue.",
    "",
    "Constraints encoded here on purpose:",
    "  * `functions` may NOT be combined with `builds` — per-lambda memory and",
    "    maxDuration therefore live in builds[].config.",
    "  * top-level `headers` may NOT be combined with `routes` — security",
    "    headers are therefore attached to the catch-all route below.",
    "",
    "Prefer this manifest for a one-click deploy. For independent scaling and",
    "independent rollback per service, use the TWO-PROJECT layout instead",
    "(frontend/vercel.json + backend/vercel.json) — see README section 16."
  ],

  "builds": [
    {
      "src": "api/index.py",
      "use": "@vercel/python",
      "config": {
        "runtime": "python3.12",
        "maxLambdaSize": "45mb",
        "memory": 1024,
        "maxDuration": 60
      }
    },
    {
      "src": "frontend/package.json",
      "use": "@vercel/next"
    }
  ],

  "routes": [
    {
      "src": "/api/health(?:/.*)?",
      "dest": "/api/index.py",
      "headers": { "Cache-Control": "no-store, max-age=0" }
    },
    {
      "src": "/api/runs/[^/]+/stream",
      "dest": "/api/index.py",
      "headers": {
        "Cache-Control": "no-store, no-transform",
        "Content-Type": "text/event-stream",
        "X-Accel-Buffering": "no"
      }
    },
    {
      "src": "/api/(?:.*)",
      "dest": "/api/index.py"
    },

    {
      "//": "FastAPI serves its docs under /api/* (docs_url='/api/docs'). These are convenience redirects so the bare paths resolve instead of falling through to the Next.js 404.",
      "src": "/docs",
      "status": 308,
      "headers": { "Location": "/api/docs" }
    },
    {
      "src": "/redoc",
      "status": 308,
      "headers": { "Location": "/api/redoc" }
    },
    {
      "src": "/openapi.json",
      "status": 308,
      "headers": { "Location": "/api/openapi.json" }
    },

    { "handle": "filesystem" },

    {
      "src": "/(.*)",
      "dest": "/frontend/$1",
      "headers": {
        "X-Content-Type-Options": "nosniff",
        "X-Frame-Options": "SAMEORIGIN",
        "Referrer-Policy": "strict-origin-when-cross-origin",
        "Permissions-Policy": "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()"
      }
    }
  ],

  "crons": [
    {
      "path": "/api/internal/tick",
      "schedule": "*/1 * * * *"
    }
  ],

  "github": { "silent": true }
}
